   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Counter-Terrorism Legislation Amendment Bill 2019 introduces a presumption against bail and parole for anyone showing support for or links to terrorist activity, including minors, and amends the continuing detention order scheme to cover terrorist offenders also serving time for non-terrorist offences while aligning national security information protections with criminal prosecutions."
